From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:56:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llama-cpp): run the encoder of encoder-decoder models
 (T5, MADLAD)

The llama.cpp backend is llama-server's code, and llama-server never runs
the encoder of an encoder-decoder model: a T5-family GGUF (MADLAD-400-3B-MT)
is decoded as if decoder-only and answers garbage (`<2cs><2cs>...`), though
the library and llama.cpp's completion tool run it correctly (llama.cpp
#5763, #26565, no upstream fix).

Carry the server change as a llama.cpp patch beside the two this backend
already applies (patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch): the prompt goes
through the encoder when the slot starts, the decoder starts from the
model's decoder start token, the prompt cache is off for such a task, and
the seq_rm probe at load encodes a token first.

Checked on CPU at llama.cpp c0fd786 with MADLAD-400-3B-MT (bf16 GGUF): 130
query translations, 120 identical to transformers' after its
clean_up_tokenization (the rest diverge greedily at one token); the prompts
tokenize identically to transformers' on all 3,078.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 .../patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch | 141 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 141 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..da312cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0003-server-encoder-decoder.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+server: run the encoder of encoder-decoder models (T5, MADLAD-400)
+
+llama-server never ran the encoder: on a T5-family GGUF it decoded the prompt
+as if the model were decoder-only and wrote `<2cs><2cs>...` (MADLAD-400-3B-MT,
+2026-09-18), while the library (llama_model_has_encoder, the ENCODE process
+type) and tools/completion run it correctly. Upstream: #5763 left server
+support as a TODO (fairydreaming's t5-server branch, Dec 2024, unmerged);
+#26565 (Aug 2026) closed stale, no PR.
+
+- launch_slot_with_task: for a model with an encoder, the prompt's tokens move
+  to the slot's encoder input and the task's prompt becomes the decoder start
+  token (BOS when the model names none); cache_prompt is off for the task.
+- update_slots, when the slot starts its prompt: the slot's sequence is
+  cleared, then the encoder reads the input in one ubatch on the slot's
+  sequence id (an input longer than n_ubatch is refused, not asserted on);
+  the decoder then runs as for any model.
+- load_model: one token is encoded before the seq_rm probe, which decodes,
+  and a T5 decoder asserts without an encoder output.
+- the encoder output is one per context (llama_cross), so more than one slot
+  is warned about: concurrent requests would read each other's.
+
+Only /completion (a raw prompt) is right for these models: a chat template
+is text they were not trained on.
+diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+index a18b754..0a817ae 100644
+--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
++++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+@@ -351,6 +351,11 @@ struct server_slot {
+     std::vector<common_adapter_lora_info> lora;
+     int32_t alora_invocation_start = -1;
+ 
++    // encoder-decoder models (T5, MADLAD): the prompt, read by the encoder
++    // (llama_process ENCODE) when the slot starts; the task's own prompt is then
++    // the decoder's start token
++    llama_tokens enc_tokens;
++
+     // sampling
+     json json_schema;
+ 
+@@ -1231,6 +1236,13 @@ private:
+ 
+         vocab = llama_model_get_vocab(model_tgt);
+ 
++        if (llama_model_has_encoder(model_tgt) && params_base.n_parallel > 1) {
++            // the encoder's output is kept once per context, not per sequence
++            // (llama_cross): a second slot's encode would overwrite the first's
++            SRV_WRN("encoder-decoder model with %d slots: its encoder output is shared by the context, "
++                    "so concurrent requests can read each other's; use 1 slot\n", params_base.n_parallel);
++        }
++
+         try {
+             decision.init(model_tgt);
+         } catch (const std::exception & e) {
+@@ -1379,6 +1391,19 @@ private:
+ 
+         slots.clear();
+ 
++        if (llama_model_has_encoder(model_tgt)) {
++            // the probe below decodes, and an encoder-decoder model's decoder reads
++            // the encoder's output (it asserts "llama_encode must be called first"):
++            // one token encoded on sequence 0 gives it that; every request encodes
++            // its own prompt over it
++            common_batch batch_enc(ctx_tgt);
++            batch_enc.add(llama_vocab_eos(vocab), 0, 0, false);
++            if (llama_process(ctx_tgt, LLAMA_PROCESS_TYPE_ENCODE, batch_enc.get()) != 0) {
++                SRV_ERR("%s", "failed to encode the probe token of an encoder-decoder model\n");
++                return false;
++            }
++        }
++
+         ctx_tgt_seq_rm_type = common_context_can_seq_rm(ctx_tgt);
+         if (ctx_tgt_seq_rm_type == COMMON_CONTEXT_SEQ_RM_TYPE_NO) {
+             SRV_WRN("%s", "speculative decoding not supported by this context\n");
+@@ -1960,6 +1985,27 @@ private:
+         // the per-request limit takes priority over the global one
+         slot.n_predict_max = task.params.n_predict != -1 ? task.params.n_predict : params_base.n_predict;
+ 
++        // an encoder-decoder model reads the prompt with its encoder, and its
++        // decoder starts from the decoder start token: the prompt moves to the
++        // slot's encoder input, and the task's prompt becomes that one token.
++        // Nothing is reused from the previous prompt: the cross-attention of
++        // every cached position belongs to another encoder input.
++        slot.enc_tokens.clear();
++        if (llama_model_has_encoder(model_tgt) && task.n_tokens() > 0) {
++            if (task.tokens.has_mtmd) {
++                send_error(task, "an encoder-decoder model takes text only", ERROR_TYPE_INVALID_REQUEST);
++                return false;
++            }
++            slot.enc_tokens = task.tokens.get_text_tokens();
++            llama_token dec_start = llama_model_decoder_start_token(model_tgt);
++            if (dec_start == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
++                dec_start = llama_vocab_bos(vocab);
++            }
++            task.tokens = server_tokens(llama_tokens{ dec_start }, false);
++            task.params.cache_prompt = false;
++            slot.prompt.clear();
++        }
++
+         slot.task = std::make_unique<const server_task>(std::move(task));
+ 
+         slot.state = slot.task->is_child()
+@@ -3650,6 +3696,39 @@ private:
+                             return;
+                         }
+ 
++                        // encoder-decoder models: the encoder reads the prompt now, right
++                        // before this slot's decoder, which attends to its output
++                        if (!slot.enc_tokens.empty()) {
++                            const int32_t n_enc = (int32_t) slot.enc_tokens.size();
++                            if (n_enc > n_ubatch) {
++                                // the encoder asserts on it: it reads the whole input in one ubatch
++                                send_error(slot,
++                                           string_format("input (%d tokens) is too large for the encoder. increase the "
++                                                         "physical batch size (current batch size: %d)", n_enc, n_ubatch),
++                                           ERROR_TYPE_EXCEED_CONTEXT_SIZE);
++                                slot.release();
++                                return;
++                            }
++                            // the previous request's decoder state goes first: the batch's
++                            // positions (0..n) are checked against what the memory holds for the
++                            // sequence, and nothing of it is reused (cache_prompt is off)
++                            slot.mem.seq_rm(slot.id, -1, -1);
++                            // the slot's own sequence id: the decoder's cross-attention mask
++                            // pairs its positions with the encoder outputs of the same sequence
++                            common_batch batch_enc(ctx_tgt);
++                            for (int32_t i = 0; i < n_enc; ++i) {
++                                batch_enc.add(slot.enc_tokens[i], i, slot.id, false);
++                            }
++                            const int32_t ret = llama_process(ctx_tgt, LLAMA_PROCESS_TYPE_ENCODE, batch_enc.get());
++                            slot.enc_tokens.clear();
++                            if (ret != 0) {
++                                send_error(slot, string_format("failed to encode the prompt (llama_process ENCODE: %d)", ret), ERROR_TYPE_SERVER);
++                                slot.release();
++                                return;
++                            }
++                            SLT_DBG(slot, "encoded %d prompt tokens\n", n_enc);
++                        }
++
+                         if (!slot.can_split()) {
+                             if (slot.task->n_tokens() > n_ubatch) {
+                                 send_error(slot,
-- 
